How this meets your goals
- Multi-page system: Separate routes for listing (/docs) and editing (/docs/[slug]). The index shows docs, search, and creation; the slug page hosts a full editor.
- Firebase integration: Firestore stores docs under collection "docs" keyed by slug; Storage stores uploaded images. Live updates via onSnapshot; create/rename/delete covered.
- MarkdownRX integration: lib/markdownrx.ts compiles markdown to sanitized, highlighted HTML. MarkdownRXPreview renders it; MarkdownRXEditor provides a Tailwind-styled editor with toolbar, split preview, and image uploads.
- Tailwind styling: Editor and pages use utility classes; optionally add @tailwindcss/typography for better rendered markdown.
- use client: All client-side components that use React state/effects are annotated with "use client" at the top.
- Alignment with existing setup: Keep your Firebase bootstrap in '@/lib/firebase'. If you already have one, merge the config fields and exports (db, storage).

Implementation notes
- Ensure .env.local includes NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_* vars and that you’ve enabled Firestore and Storage in Firebase.
- In tailwind.config.js, enable the typography plugin and ensure content globs include app, components, and lib.
- For role-based access, add Firebase Auth and guard writes accordingly.
- For SEO/static export of docs, you can generate static pages by reading Firestore server-side if desired.

Below is a clear design and implementation for a multi-page documentation system in a Next.js (App Router) app that uses Firebase (Firestore + Storage), Tailwind CSS, and a MarkdownRX engine for rendering/preview. It also ensures your editor component aligns with proper documentation formatting requirements by:
- Providing a documentation-friendly toolbar (headings, lists, tables, code blocks, links, images).
- Enforcing formatting on save (single H1 derived from title, tidy front matter-like header, normalize blank lines and EOF newline).
- Displaying a live Outline of headings to encourage proper structure.
- Using Tailwind Typography (prose) for readable documentation.

What you’ll get
- Pages:
  - /docs: list, search, create
  - /docs/[slug]: edit document, preview, outline, rename, delete
- Firebase integration:
  - Firestore: docs collection {title, content, tags, createdAt, updatedAt}
  - Storage: image uploads under docs/{slug}/images/*
- MarkdownRX Integration:
  - lib/markdownrx.ts provides markdownToHtml
  - components/MarkdownRX.tsx provides Preview and Editor (with toolbar and modes)
- Editor formatting alignment:
  - Toolbar with semantic elements
  - Format-on-save normalization (single H1 from title, EOF newline, normalized spacing)
  - Outline panel to guide structure
  - Typography styles through className="prose max-w-none"

Assumptions
- Your Firebase is already initialized and exported as db (Firestore) and storage (Storage) from "@/lib/firebase".
- Tailwind is configured; add @tailwindcss/typography plugin for better preview, then apply prose class.

Key steps (non-duplicative excerpts)
1) Multi-page routing structure (App Router)
- app/docs/page.tsx: list/search/create docs (client page for interactivity; remember to add "use client").
- app/docs/[slug]/page.tsx: loads a DocEditor client component by slug.

Example: app/docs/page.tsx (concise)
"use client";
import * as React from "react";
import { db } from "@/lib/firebase";
import { collection, query, orderBy, limit, onSnapshot, addDoc, serverTimestamp } from "firebase/firestore";
import Link from "next/link";

export default function DocsIndexPage() {
  const [docs, setDocs] = React.useState<any[]>([]);
  const [qText, setQText] = React.useState("");
  const [creating, setCreating] = React.useState(false);

  React.useEffect(() => {
    const q = query(collection(db, "docs"), orderBy("updatedAt", "desc"), limit(100));
    const unsub = onSnapshot(q, (snap) => {
      const rows = snap.docs.map((d) => ({ id: d.id, ...d.data() }));
      setDocs(rows);
    });
    return () => unsub();
  }, []);

  async function onCreate() {
    if (creating) return;
    setCreating(true);
    const title = prompt("Title for new doc?")?.trim();
    if (!title) { setCreating(false); return; }
    const slug = title.toLowerCase().replace(/[^a-z0-9]+/g, "-").replace(/(^-|-$)+/g, "");
    await addDoc(collection(db, "docs"), { __slug: slug, title, content: `# ${title}\n\n`, createdAt: serverTimestamp(), updatedAt: serverTimestamp(), tags: [] });
    setCreating(false);
  }

  const filtered = qText ? docs.filter(d => (d.title||"").toLowerCase().includes(qText.toLowerCase())) : docs;

  return (
    <div className="p-6 space-y-4">
      <div className="flex gap-2 items-center">
        <input className="border rounded px-3 py-2 w-full" placeholder="Search docs…" value={qText} onChange={(e)=>setQText(e.target.value)} />
        <button className="border rounded px-3 py-2" onClick={onCreate} disabled={creating}>New</button>
      </div>
      <ul className="divide-y">
        {filtered.map((d) => (
          <li key={d.id} className="py-3 flex items-center justify-between">
            <div>
              <div className="font-medium">{d.title}</div>
              <div className="text-sm text-gray-500">{d.tags?.join(", ")}</div>
            </div>
            <Link className="text-blue-600 underline" href={`/docs/${d.__slug ?? d.id}`}>Open</Link>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    </div>
  );
}

2) MarkdownRX integration for rendering/preview
- Use a unified/remark/rehype pipeline via markdownToHtml in a Preview component. Render in client components and apply className="prose max-w-none" for documentation-friendly output.

3) Documentation editor component (client) with formatting alignment
- Provide a semantic toolbar: headings, bold/italic, lists, code, tables, links, images.
- Implement format-on-save to enforce constraints:
  - Single H1 equals the Title input.
  - Normalize blank lines between blocks and ensure trailing newline.
- Provide an Outline panel listing headings from current content to guide structure.

Editor skeleton (concise)
"use client";
import * as React from "react";
import { MarkdownRXPreview } from "@/components/MarkdownRX";

type Props = { value: string; onChange: (v: string) => void; onUploadImage?: (f: File) => Promise<string>; };

export function DocMarkdownEditor({ value, onChange, onUploadImage }: Props) {
  const [mode, setMode] = React.useState<"edit"|"preview"|"split">("split");
  const taRef = React.useRef<HTMLTextAreaElement|null>(null);

  function insert(snippet: string) {
    const ta = taRef.current; if (!ta) return;
    const s = ta.selectionStart ?? 0; const e = ta.selectionEnd ?? 0;
    const next = value.slice(0, s) + snippet + value.slice(e);
    onChange(next);
    requestAnimationFrame(()=>{ ta.focus(); ta.setSelectionRange(s+snippet.length, s+snippet.length); });
  }

  function wrap(before: string, after = before) {
    const ta = taRef.current; if (!ta) return;
    const s = ta.selectionStart ?? 0; const e = ta.selectionEnd ?? 0;
    const sel = value.slice(s, e);
    const next = value.slice(0, s) + before + sel + after + value.slice(e);
    onChange(next);
    requestAnimationFrame(()=>{ ta.focus(); const c = s + before.length + sel.length + after.length; ta.setSelectionRange(c, c); });
  }

  async function onPickImage(e: React.ChangeEvent<HTMLInputElement>) {
    const file = e.target.files?.[0];
    if (!file || !onUploadImage) return;
    const url = await onUploadImage(file);
    insert(`![${file.name.replace(/\..+$/, "")}](${url})`);
    e.target.value = "";
  }

  const outline = React.useMemo(() => {
    return (value || "").split(/\n/)
      .map((l, i) => { const m = /^(#{1,6})\s+(.*)/.exec(l); return m ? { level: m[1].length, text: m[2], i } : null; })
      .filter(Boolean) as { level: number; text: string; i: number }[];
  }, [value]);

  return (
    <div className="border rounded-md overflow-hidden">
      <div className="flex items-center gap-2 border-b px-2 py-2 bg-muted/40">
        <button className="border rounded px-2 py-1 text-sm" onClick={()=>insert("# ")}>H1</button>
        <button className="border rounded px-2 py-1 text-sm" onClick={()=>insert("## ")}>H2</button>
        <button className="border rounded px-2 py-1 text-sm" onClick={()=>insert("### ")}>H3</button>
        <button className="border rounded px-2 py-1 text-sm" onClick={()=>wrap("**","**")}>Bold</button>
        <button className="border rounded px-2 py-1 text-sm" onClick={()=>wrap("_","_")}>Italic</button>
        <button className="border rounded px-2 py-1 text-sm" onClick={()=>wrap("`","`")}>Code</button>
        <button className="border rounded px-2 py-1 text-sm" onClick={()=>insert("> ")}>Quote</button>
        <button className="border rounded px-2 py-1 text-sm" onClick={()=>insert("- ")}>UL</button>
        <button className="border rounded px-2 py-1 text-sm" onClick={()=>insert("1. ")}>OL</button>
        <button className="border rounded px-2 py-1 text-sm" onClick={()=>wrap("```\n","\n```")}>Code Block</button>
        <button className="border rounded px-2 py-1 text-sm" onClick={()=>insert("| Col A | Col B |\n| --- | --- |\n|  |  |\n")}>Table</button>
        <label className="border rounded px-2 py-1 text-sm cursor-pointer">Image<input type="file" accept="image/*" className="hidden" onChange={onPickImage} /></label>
        <div className="ml-auto flex gap-1">
          <button className={`border rounded px-2 py-1 text-sm ${mode==='edit'?'bg-primary text-white':''}`} onClick={()=>setMode('edit')}>Edit</button>
          <button className={`border rounded px-2 py-1 text-sm ${mode==='preview'?'bg-primary text-white':''}`} onClick={()=>setMode('preview')}>Preview</button>
          <button className={`border rounded px-2 py-1 text-sm ${mode==='split'?'bg-primary text-white':''}`} onClick={()=>setMode('split')}>Split</button>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div className="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-[1fr_300px]">
        {mode !== 'preview' && (
          <textarea ref={taRef} value={value} onChange={(e)=>onChange(e.target.value)} className="h-[60vh] w-full resize-none p-3 outline-none" placeholder="# Write your documentation..." />
        )}
        {mode !== 'edit' && (
          <div className="p-3 border-l overflow-auto h-[60vh]"><div className="prose max-w-none"><MarkdownRXPreview value={value} /></div></div>
        )}
        <div className="border-l p-3 hidden md:block">
          <div className="font-semibold mb-2">Outline</div>
          <ul className="space-y-1 text-sm">
            {outline.map((h, idx) => (
              <li key={idx} style={{ paddingLeft: (h.level - 1) * 8 }}>{`${"#".repeat(h.level)} ${h.text}`}</li>
            ))}
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  );
}

4) Using Firebase in the editor page (/docs/[slug])
- Load and live-subscribe to the document by slug.
- Save with serverTimestamp.
- Handle image uploads to Storage and insert returned URL in markdown.
- Implement format-on-save to align with documentation requirements.

app/docs/[slug]/page.tsx (client)
"use client";
import * as React from "react";
import { useRouter, useParams } from "next/navigation";
import { db, storage } from "@/lib/firebase";
import { collection, query, where, limit, onSnapshot, updateDoc, serverTimestamp } from "firebase/firestore";
import { doc as fsDoc } from "firebase/firestore";
import { ref, uploadBytes, getDownloadURL } from "firebase/storage";
import { DocMarkdownEditor } from "@/components/DocMarkdownEditor";

function normalizeForSave(title: string, md: string) {
  const lines = md.split(/\n/);
  const rest = lines.filter(l => !/^#\s/.test(l));
  const h1 = `# ${title}`;
  let out = [h1, "", ...rest].join("\n");
  out = out.replace(/\n{3,}/g, "\n\n");
  if (!out.endsWith("\n")) out += "\n";
  return out;
}

export default function DocPage() {
  const { slug } = useParams() as { slug: string };
  const router = useRouter();
  const [title, setTitle] = React.useState("");
  const [content, setContent] = React.useState("");
  const [docId, setDocId] = React.useState<string|undefined>();

  React.useEffect(() => {
    const q = query(collection(db, "docs"), where("__slug", "==", slug), limit(1));
    const unsub = onSnapshot(q, (snap) => {
      if (snap.empty) return;
      const d = snap.docs[0];
      setDocId(d.id);
      const data: any = d.data();
      setTitle(data.title || "");
      setContent(data.content || "");
    });
    return () => unsub();
  }, [slug]);

  async function onSave() {
    if (!docId) return;
    const contentOut = normalizeForSave(title, content);
    await updateDoc(fsDoc(db, "docs", docId), {
      title,
      content: contentOut,
      updatedAt: serverTimestamp(),
    });
  }

  async function onUploadImage(file: File) {
    const path = `docs/${slug}/images/${Date.now()}-${file.name}`;
    const r = ref(storage, path);
    await uploadBytes(r, file, { contentType: file.type });
    return await getDownloadURL(r);
  }

  return (
    <div className="p-6 space-y-4">
      <div className="flex items-center gap-2">
        <input className="border rounded px-3 py-2 w-full" value={title} onChange={(e)=>setTitle(e.target.value)} placeholder="Document title" />
        <button className="border rounded px-3 py-2" onClick={onSave}>Save</button>
      </div>
      <DocMarkdownEditor value={content} onChange={setContent} onUploadImage={onUploadImage} />
    </div>
  );
}

5) Notes on client components and hooks
- Place "use client" at the top of files that use React hooks like useState/useEffect or Next.js client hooks (useRouter, useParams).
- Server components can wrap pages and pass props to client children when needed.

6) Ensuring proper documentation formatting
- Enforce a single H1 from the title in normalizeForSave.
- Encourage sectioning via the Outline panel.
- Use Tailwind Typography (prose) for readable, consistent output.
- Optionally add lint hints (e.g., warn on missing H2s, excessively long lines) before saving.

With these pieces, you have a two-page docs system, MarkdownRX for rendering, a Tailwind-styled editor with a semantic toolbar and outline, and Firebase for persistence and media uploads, all using client-side hooks correctly with "use client" where required.

#include <bits/stdc++.h>
using namespace std;

using ll = long long;
const ll INF = (ll)4e18;

struct Edge {int to; int w;};

vector<ll> dijkstra(int n, int src, const vector<vector<Edge>>& g){
    vector<ll> dist(n+1, INF);
    priority_queue<pair<ll,int>, vector<pair<ll,int>>, greater<pair<ll,int>>> pq;
    dist[src]=0; pq.push({0, src});
    while(!pq.empty()){
        auto [d,u]=pq.top(); pq.pop();
        if(d!=dist[u]) continue;
        for(const auto &e: g[u]){
            int v=e.to; ll nd=d+e.w;
            if(nd<dist[v]){ dist[v]=nd; pq.push({nd,v}); }
        }
    }
    return dist;
}

int main(){
    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);
    cin.tie(nullptr);

    int n,m,k;
    if(!(cin>>n>>m>>k)) return 0;
    vector<vector<Edge>> g(n+1);
    for(int i=0;i<m;++i){
        int u,v; int w; cin>>u>>v>>w;
        g[u].push_back({v,w});
        g[v].push_back({u,w});
    }

    // Precompute shortest path distances in kilometers from 1 and from n
    vector<ll> d1 = dijkstra(n, 1, g);
    vector<ll> dn = dijkstra(n, n, g);

    // For each day, read speeds (seconds per km), compute minimal waiting time
    // Waiting time for meeting at node i is abs(a*d1[i] - b*dn[i])
    // We need min over i.
    for(int day=0; day<k; ++day){
        ll a,b; cin>>a>>b;
        ll best = INF;
        for(int i=1;i<=n;++i){
            if(d1[i]==INF || dn[i]==INF) continue; // unreachable, though graph guarantees path 1..n
            // Use 128-bit to prevent overflow: (up to 1e6 * path up to ~1e11) => 1e17 fits in 64, but safe.
            __int128 t1 = (__int128)a * d1[i];
            __int128 t2 = (__int128)b * dn[i];
            __int128 diff = t1 - t2; if(diff<0) diff = -diff;
            ll val = (ll)diff; // fits since a<=1e6, dist<=1e11 => 1e17 < 2^63
            if(val < best) best = val;
        }
        cout<<best<<"\n";
    }
    return 0;
}

Below is a complete, self-contained Tkinter application that manages the tournament’s scoring. It is organized, validated, and commented for maintainability. It includes:
- Participants (Teams and Individuals) with “one event only” support and optional chosen event.
- Events (Team or Individual) with optional per-event points.
- Results entry per event via ranked ordering with strong validation.
- Leaderboards for teams and individuals.
- Points configuration (global schemes + custom editor).
- Save/Load/New via JSON with validation and clear error handling.

To run: save as a .py file and execute with Python 3.8+.

```python
aimport json
from dataclasses import dataclass, asdict, field
from typing import Dict, List, Optional, Tuple

import tkinter as tk
from tkinter import ttk, messagebox, filedialog


# -------------------------
# Data Model
# -------------------------

@dataclass
class Team:
    id: int
    name: str
    members: List[str] = field(default_factory=list)
    one_event_only: bool = False
    chosen_event_id: Optional[int] = None  # Applies if one_event_only is True


@dataclass
class Individual:
    id: int
    name: str
    one_event_only: bool = False
    chosen_event_id: Optional[int] = None  # Applies if one_event_only is True


@dataclass
class Event:
    id: int
    name: str
    type: str  # "Team" or "Individual"
    genre: str = ""
    points_map: Optional[Dict[int, int]] = None  # Per-event override


class TournamentData:
    """
    Core model for the tournament. Handles validation, CRUD operations,
    results storage, points aggregation, and JSON (de)serialization.
    """
    def __init__(self):
        self.teams: Dict[int, Team] = {}
        self.individuals: Dict[int, Individual] = {}
        self.events: Dict[int, Event] = {}
        # event_id -> ordered list of entrant IDs
        self.results: Dict[int, List[int]] = {}
        # Global points table (default: F1 Top 10)
        self.points_map: Dict[int, int] = {
            1: 25, 2: 18, 3: 15, 4: 12, 5: 10, 6: 8, 7: 6, 8: 4, 9: 2, 10: 1
        }
        self.team_counter = 1
        self.indiv_counter = 1
        self.event_counter = 1

    # ---- Constraints ----
    def max_teams(self) -> int:
        return 4

    def max_team_members(self) -> int:
        return 5

    def max_individuals(self) -> int:
        return 20

    def max_events_per_type(self) -> int:
        # 5 Team events and 5 Individual events
        return 5

    # ---- Helpers ----
    @staticmethod
    def _clean_name(value: str) -> str:
        return (value or "").strip()

    def _validate_points_map(self, points: Dict[int, int]) -> None:
        if not isinstance(points, dict) or not points:
            raise ValueError("Points map must be a non-empty dictionary.")
        for k, v in points.items():
            if not isinstance(k, int) or k <= 0:
                raise ValueError("Rank keys must be positive integers.")
            if not isinstance(v, int) or v < 0:
                raise ValueError("Point values must be non-negative integers.")
        # Non-increasing across ranks: points[1] >= points[2] >= ...
        prev_points = None
        for r in sorted(points.keys()):
            if prev_points is not None and points[r] > prev_points:
                raise ValueError("Points should not increase for lower ranks.")
            prev_points = points[r]

    def get_points_for_event(self, event_id: int) -> Dict[int, int]:
        ev = self.events.get(event_id)
        if ev and ev.points_map:
            return ev.points_map
        return self.points_map

    # ---- CRUD for Teams ----
    def add_team(self, name: str, members: List[str], one_event_only: bool = False, chosen_event_id: Optional[int] = None) -> int:
        name = self._clean_name(name)
        if not name:
            raise ValueError("Team name cannot be empty.")
        if len(self.teams) >= self.max_teams():
            raise ValueError("Maximum number of teams reached (4).")
        if len(members) > self.max_team_members():
            raise ValueError("A team can have at most 5 members.")
        cleaned_members = [self._clean_name(m) for m in members if self._clean_name(m)]
        if not cleaned_members:
            raise ValueError("A team must have at least one member.")
        if any(t.name.lower() == name.lower() for t in self.teams.values()):
            raise ValueError("Team name must be unique.")
        if chosen_event_id is not None:
            ev = self.events.get(chosen_event_id)
            if ev is None or ev.type != "Team":
                raise ValueError("Chosen event must be a valid Team event.")
        team_id = self.team_counter
        self.team_counter += 1
        self.teams[team_id] = Team(id=team_id, name=name, members=cleaned_members,
                                   one_event_only=one_event_only, chosen_event_id=chosen_event_id)
        return team_id

    def edit_team(self, tid: int, name: str, members: List[str], one_event_only: bool, chosen_event_id: Optional[int]) -> None:
        if tid not in self.teams:
            raise ValueError("Team not found.")
        name = self._clean_name(name)
        if not name:
            raise ValueError("Team name cannot be empty.")
        if len(members) > self.max_team_members():
            raise ValueError("A team can have at most 5 members.")
        cleaned_members = [self._clean_name(m) for m in members if self._clean_name(m)]
        if not cleaned_members:
            raise ValueError("A team must have at least one member.")
        if chosen_event_id is not None:
            ev = self.events.get(chosen_event_id)
            if ev is None or ev.type != "Team":
                raise ValueError("Chosen event must be a valid Team event.")
        if any(t.name.lower() == name.lower() and t.id != tid for t in self.teams.values()):
            raise ValueError("Team name must be unique.")
        t = self.teams[tid]
        t.name = name
        t.members = cleaned_members
        t.one_event_only = one_event_only
        t.chosen_event_id = chosen_event_id

    def remove_team(self, tid: int) -> None:
        if tid not in self.teams:
            raise ValueError("Team not found.")
        # Remove from any Team event results
        for ev_id, places in list(self.results.items()):
            ev = self.events.get(ev_id)
            if ev and ev.type == "Team":
                self.results[ev_id] = [pid for pid in places if pid != tid]
        del self.teams[tid]

    # ---- CRUD for Individuals ----
    def add_individual(self, name: str, one_event_only: bool = False, chosen_event_id: Optional[int] = None) -> int:
        name = self._clean_name(name)
        if not name:
            raise ValueError("Individual name cannot be empty.")
        if len(self.individuals) >= self.max_individuals():
            raise ValueError("Maximum number of individuals reached (20).")
        if any(i.name.lower() == name.lower() for i in self.individuals.values()):
            raise ValueError("Individual name must be unique.")
        if chosen_event_id is not None:
            ev = self.events.get(chosen_event_id)
            if ev is None or ev.type != "Individual":
                raise ValueError("Chosen event must be a valid Individual event.")
        iid = self.indiv_counter
        self.indiv_counter += 1
        self.individuals[iid] = Individual(id=iid, name=name,
                                           one_event_only=one_event_only, chosen_event_id=chosen_event_id)
        return iid

    def edit_individual(self, iid: int, name: str, one_event_only: bool, chosen_event_id: Optional[int]) -> None:
        if iid not in self.individuals:
            raise ValueError("Individual not found.")
        name = self._clean_name(name)
        if not name:
            raise ValueError("Individual name cannot be empty.")
        if chosen_event_id is not None:
            ev = self.events.get(chosen_event_id)
            if ev is None or ev.type != "Individual":
                raise ValueError("Chosen event must be a valid Individual event.")
        if any(p.name.lower() == name.lower() and p.id != iid for p in self.individuals.values()):
            raise ValueError("Individual name must be unique.")
        person = self.individuals[iid]
        person.name = name
        person.one_event_only = one_event_only
        person.chosen_event_id = chosen_event_id

    def remove_individual(self, iid: int) -> None:
        if iid not in self.individuals:
            raise ValueError("Individual not found.")
        for ev_id, places in list(self.results.items()):
            ev = self.events.get(ev_id)
            if ev and ev.type == "Individual":
                self.results[ev_id] = [pid for pid in places if pid != iid]
        del self.individuals[iid]

    # ---- CRUD for Events ----
    def add_event(self, name: str, etype: str, genre: str = "", points_map: Optional[Dict[int, int]] = None) -> int:
        name = self._clean_name(name)
        if not name:
            raise ValueError("Event name cannot be empty.")
        if etype not in ("Team", "Individual"):
            raise ValueError("Event type must be 'Team' or 'Individual'.")
        count_type = sum(1 for e in self.events.values() if e.type == etype)
        if count_type >= self.max_events_per_type():
            raise ValueError(f"Maximum number of {etype} events reached (5).")
        if any(e.name.lower() == name.lower() for e in self.events.values()):
            raise ValueError("Event name must be unique.")
        if points_map:
            self._validate_points_map(points_map)
        eid = self.event_counter
        self.event_counter += 1
        self.events[eid] = Event(id=eid, name=name, type=etype, genre=self._clean_name(genre), points_map=points_map)
        return eid

    def edit_event(self, eid: int, name: str, etype: str, genre: str, points_map: Optional[Dict[int, int]]) -> None:
        if eid not in self.events:
            raise ValueError("Event not found.")
        name = self._clean_name(name)
        if not name:
            raise ValueError("Event name cannot be empty.")
        if etype not in ("Team", "Individual"):
            raise ValueError("Event type must be 'Team' or 'Individual'.")
        if any(e.name.lower() == name.lower() and e.id != eid for e in self.events.values()):
            raise ValueError("Event name must be unique.")
        if points_map:
            self._validate_points_map(points_map)
        old = self.events[eid]
        # If the type changes, clear any existing results (to avoid cross-type mismatch)
        if old.type != etype and eid in self.results:
            self.results[eid] = []
        old.name = name
        old.type = etype
        old.genre = self._clean_name(genre)
        old.points_map = points_map

    def remove_event(self, eid: int) -> None:
        if eid not in self.events:
            raise ValueError("Event not found.")
        # Remove results for this event
        self.results.pop(eid, None)
        # Clear chosen_event_id references
        for t in self.teams.values():
            if t.chosen_event_id == eid:
                t.chosen_event_id = None
        for i in self.individuals.values():
            if i.chosen_event_id == eid:
                i.chosen_event_id = None
        del self.events[eid]

    # ---- Results and Scoring ----
    def set_event_results(self, eid: int, ordered_ids: List[int]) -> None:
        if eid not in self.events:
            raise ValueError("Event not found.")
        ev = self.events[eid]
        # Validate entrants belong to the correct population
        population = self.teams if ev.type == "Team" else self.individuals
        seen = set()
        for pid in ordered_ids:
            if pid not in population:
                raise ValueError("Results contain an unknown entrant.")
            if pid in seen:
                raise ValueError("Duplicate entrant in results order.")
            # One-event-only validation
            entrant = population[pid]
            if getattr(entrant, 'one_event_only', False):
                if entrant.chosen_event_id is None:
                    entrant.chosen_event_id = eid
                elif entrant.chosen_event_id != eid:
                    raise ValueError(f"Entrant '{getattr(entrant,'name','')}' is limited to one event only and already assigned to another event.")
            seen.add(pid)
        self.results[eid] = ordered_ids.copy()

    def clear_event_results(self, eid: int) -> None:
        self.results.pop(eid, None)

    def compute_leaderboards(self) -> Tuple[List[Tuple[str, int]], List[Tuple[str, int]]]:
        team_points: Dict[int, int] = {tid: 0 for tid in self.teams}
        indiv_points: Dict[int, int] = {iid: 0 for iid in self.individuals}
        for eid, order in self.results.items():
            ev = self.events.get(eid)
            if not ev:
                continue
            pmap = self.get_points_for_event(eid)
            for rank, pid in enumerate(order, start=1):
                pts = pmap.get(rank, 0)
                if ev.type == "Team":
                    if pid in team_points:
                        team_points[pid] += pts
                else:
                    if pid in indiv_points:
                        indiv_points[pid] += pts
        team_lb = sorted([(self.teams[tid].name, pts) for tid, pts in team_points.items()], key=lambda x: (-x[1], x[0].lower()))
        indiv_lb = sorted([(self.individuals[iid].name, pts) for iid, pts in indiv_points.items()], key=lambda x: (-x[1], x[0].lower()))
        return team_lb, indiv_lb

    # ---- Serialization ----
    def to_json(self) -> str:
        data = {
            'teams': [asdict(t) for t in self.teams.values()],
            'individuals': [asdict(i) for i in self.individuals.values()],
            'events': [asdict(e) for e in self.events.values()],
            'results': {str(eid): order for eid, order in self.results.items()},
            'points_map': self.points_map,
            'counters': {
                'team': self.team_counter,
                'individual': self.indiv_counter,
                'event': self.event_counter
            }
        }
        return json.dumps(data, indent=2)

    @staticmethod
    def from_json(text: str) -> 'TournamentData':
        obj = json.loads(text)
        td = TournamentData()
        td.points_map = {int(k) if isinstance(k, str) else k: int(v) for k, v in obj.get('points_map', {}).items()} or td.points_map
        for t in obj.get('teams', []):
            td.teams[t['id']] = Team(**t)
        for p in obj.get('individuals', []):
            td.individuals[p['id']] = Individual(**p)
        for e in obj.get('events', []):
            # Convert keys of points_map to int if present
            if e.get('points_map'):
                e['points_map'] = {int(k) if isinstance(k, str) else k: int(v) for k, v in e['points_map'].items()}
            td.events[e['id']] = Event(**e)
        td.results = {int(eid): order for eid, order in obj.get('results', {}).items()}
        counters = obj.get('counters', {})
        td.team_counter = max([1] + [t.id for t in td.teams.values()]) + 1
        td.indiv_counter = max([1] + [i.id for i in td.individuals.values()]) + 1
        td.event_counter = max([1] + [e.id for e in td.events.values()]) + 1
        # Override with stored counters if larger (to avoid collisions)
        td.team_counter = max(td.team_counter, int(counters.get('team', td.team_counter)))
        td.indiv_counter = max(td.indiv_counter, int(counters.get('individual', td.indiv_counter)))
        td.event_counter = max(td.event_counter, int(counters.get('event', td.event_counter)))
        return td


